### EcomfyApp Mini Lead Routing Engine — REST collection
### Use with the VS Code "REST Client" extension, or copy as curl.
@base = http://localhost:8000

### Health
GET {{base}}/health

### Reset demo (fresh buyers + cleared data)
POST {{base}}/dev/reset

### Seed all 10 fixture leads through the real pipeline
POST {{base}}/dev/seed-leads

### 1. Valid lead -> SOLD to first eligible buyer (TX / auto_insurance)
POST {{base}}/leads
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "first_name": "John", "last_name": "Smith",
  "phone": "2145550100", "email": "first@example.com",
  "state": "TX", "vertical": "auto_insurance",
  "source": "web_form", "jornaya_lead_id": "JRN-1"
}

### 2. Lead SOLD after fallback (FL / life -> B reject, C timeout, A accept)
POST {{base}}/leads
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "first_name": "Maria", "last_name": "Gonzalez",
  "phone": "3055550200", "email": "fallback@example.com",
  "state": "FL", "vertical": "life_insurance",
  "source": "web_form", "trusted_form_cert_url": "https://cert/x"
}

### 3. Duplicate -> REJECTED (re-send #1 phone/email)
POST {{base}}/leads
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "first_name": "John", "last_name": "Smith",
  "phone": "2145550100", "email": "first@example.com",
  "state": "TX", "vertical": "auto_insurance",
  "source": "web_form", "jornaya_lead_id": "JRN-2"
}

### 4. Missing email -> REJECTED
POST {{base}}/leads
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "first_name": "Carlos", "phone": "3055550400", "email": "",
  "state": "FL", "vertical": "life_insurance",
  "source": "web_form", "trusted_form_cert_url": "https://cert/x"
}

### 5 & 6. Discards: buyer_d (insufficient balance), buyer_e (cap reached) — see evaluations[]
POST {{base}}/leads
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "first_name": "Eval", "last_name": "Trace",
  "phone": "3055550500", "email": "eval@example.com",
  "state": "FL", "vertical": "life_insurance",
  "source": "web_form", "trusted_form_cert_url": "https://cert/x"
}

### 7. No eligible buyers -> UNSOLD (WA)
POST {{base}}/leads
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "first_name": "Sophia", "phone": "2065551000", "email": "wa@example.com",
  "state": "WA", "vertical": "life_insurance",
  "source": "web_form", "trusted_form_cert_url": "https://cert/x"
}

### 8a. Sell a lead to return
POST {{base}}/leads
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "first_name": "Ret", "last_name": "User",
  "phone": "2145550800", "email": "ret@example.com",
  "state": "TX", "vertical": "auto_insurance",
  "source": "web_form", "jornaya_lead_id": "JRN-8"
}

### 8b. Return it (replace LEAD_ID with the id from 8a) -> refund
POST {{base}}/leads/LEAD_ID/return
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "wrong number" }

### Lead detail (full trace: evaluations + attempts + ledger)
GET {{base}}/leads/LEAD_ID

### Daily operational summary
GET {{base}}/reports/daily-summary

### Daily summary WITH AI executive summary (needs ANTHROPIC_API_KEY)
GET {{base}}/reports/daily-summary?ai=true

### Buyers / Leads / Alerts
GET {{base}}/buyers
###
GET {{base}}/leads?limit=50
###
GET {{base}}/alerts
